Z||000000||frontal lobe||01-06-2001||12:57 AM||||I did a "Griswald's" and loaded up the minivan and drove the family 1400 miles to Florida to see the in-laws for Christmas.  So I'm cruising down I-75 around Tampa at about 82 mph.  I like to get in the left lane, pass, and get back over.  Apparently someone thought I pulled back in too soon because even though I was pulling away from them, they suddenly went roaring past me and drove far ahead.  I kept driving at the same speed and about 5 minutes later I came upon the same car and passed them again.  This time the person came roaring up and then drove along next to me for a while, then passed but pulled in front of me and slowed down.  So I had to go around and pass again.  Same thing.  Then one time while passing, the person sped up and wouldn't let me pass and drove along side on the right.  Finally the person started crossing the line slowly coming door to door to me in my (the left)lane.  Then the person suddenly got back in the right lane and sped off.<P>About a 1/2 hour later I'm coming up on 3 cars in the right lane.  I start passing them.  The 2 cars in front slow down and the 3rd car turns on his left turn signal and wants to come over.  I'm already almost on the guys rear bumper in the left lane and the 2 cars are getting off on an exit and so are clearing the lane in front of him so I don't let him over and just keep going.  The guy BARELY had to slow down.  But THAT person comes roaring up on me to and drives along side for quite awhile, then finally cuts me off so I have to slow down, and then floors it and takes off.<P>I don't know if I was supposed to SEE them or not, but I couldn't because it was almost midnight so dark.  Maybe I should have been afraid but I wasn't, but my wife was.<P>Gotta love that road rage.||||reg||1
