Z||000020||Sillhouette.com||01-08-2001||10:02 PM||||Actually I bought it in Germany about five years ago.  It's called Clifford AvantGuard III.  There are much more advanced designs out there these days. My has other functions such as remote start through the same phone number except instead of KILL you type in START.  It's also hooked up to the stereo system gives out an ear piercing sound that will do damage in 5s about 150dB sound.  Close / Open windows while away Valet mode where only one door opens.  If any other doors are attempted the car shuts off. It has a pager that beeps your through either a cell or a pager if the alarm is tripped.  <P>The new one can be hooked up to central monitoring place and they can find your car or help you in distress something like on the Cadillac STS On Star.  <P>For price ask around stereo places and have them install it otherwise they will not insure your car.  Last I heard something like this installed in Toronto was 1500 dollars (Art of Noise)<P>Later<p>[This message has been edited by Sillhouette.com (edited 01-08-2001).]||||reg||1
